; In-tree unit + integration tests for smt/combine. Stays within the smt/ tree, so it
; honors the dependency firewall (I3 — nothing above the OCaml stdlib). Run via
; `make combine-test`; also built by `make build`.
;
; The toy EUF (a naive congruence closure) and toy LIA (a brute-force bounded-integer
; decision procedure) here are deliberately test-only, written from the theory specs alone
; (DESIGN §10): they share no code with the real engines, and — like the naive oracles in
; euf/lia — give an independent cross-check of the combinator's end-to-end N-O behavior.
; The mini DPLL(T) driver stands in for the CDCL(T) seam so the split lifecycle is
; exercised. Now that the sibling adapters are merged, the SAME functorized driver ALSO
; binds the real Euf_adapter + Lia_adapter (Part 3 — the empirical W1 gate), so this exe
; additionally links oxsmt_euf + oxsmt_lia. The library oxsmt_combine itself stays
; core-only (engine-independent); only this test reaches for the concrete adapters.

(executable
 (name combine_test)
 (modules combine_test)
 (libraries oxsmt_core oxsmt_combine oxsmt_euf oxsmt_lia))

(executable
 (name lia_eq_prop_combine_test)
 (modules lia_eq_prop_combine_test)
 (libraries oxsmt_core oxsmt_combine oxsmt_euf oxsmt_lia))

(executable
 (name binary_interface_router_test)
 (modules binary_interface_router_test)
 (libraries oxsmt_core oxsmt_combine))
